{
  "raw": {
    "https://irp.cdn-website.com/62fe7d2a/files/uploaded/Biology+new+8.6.26.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology.  \n \n \nFull-Time Position \nAssistant Professor of Biology \n \nUnion Commonwealth University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of \nBiology beginning August 11, 2026. \nThe successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate \nteaching, student mentoring, academic advising, curriculum development, recruitment and \nretention, scholarly and professional development appropriate to the appointment, and service to \nthe Department, School, and University. \nApplicants from diverse academic and professional backgrounds are encouraged to apply, \nincluding those with expertise in the biological sciences, biomedical sciences, medicine, nursing, \nand other health-related disciplines. \nApplicants with an earned terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent) in Biology or a closely related \ndiscipline, as outlined in the Qualifications for Tenure-Track Appointment section below, are \neligible for appointment to a tenure-track position. Candidates with a master's degree in Biology \nor a related field may be considered for a full-time, non-tenure-track appointment. Additionally, \nindividuals with appropriate graduate credentials and substantial professional experience in a \nhealth-related discipline, including medicine, nursing, physician assistant studies, or allied \nhealth, who are academically qualified to teach biology courses, are encouraged to apply and \nmay also be considered for a full-time, non-tenure-track appointment. \nPosition Responsibilities \nThe successful candidate will: \n Teach undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses in biology based on departmental \nneeds and the candidate's areas of expertise. \n Teach foundational courses such as General Biology, Human Biology, Anatomy and \nPhysiology, Microbiology, Cell Biology, Genetics, Ecology, Evolution, and upper-level \nbiology courses as assigned. \n Develop engaging learning experiences that integrate scientific principles with practical \napplications and current biological research. \n Foster critical thinking, scientific inquiry, laboratory skills, and evidence-based decision \nmaking. \n Advise and mentor biology majors and students pursuing careers in healthcare, medicine, \nnursing, education, research, environmental sciences, and other life science professions. \n Participate in curriculum assessment, program development, student recruitment, and \nacademic advising. \n Contribute to departmental, university, and professional service activities. \n \n \n Maintain an active program of professional development, scholarship, research, or \nclinical practice appropriate to the discipline. \n Collaborate with faculty across academic programs to support interdisciplinary teaching \nand student success. \nRequired Qualifications \nApplicants must possess: \n An earned master's degree or higher in Biology, Biomedical Sciences, Medicine, Nursing \n(ARNP), Physiology, Microbiology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or another closely related \nlife science discipline by the time of appointment. \n Evidence of successful college-level teaching or demonstrated potential for excellence in \nundergraduate instruction. \n Ability to teach introductory biology and contribute across multiple areas of the \nundergraduate biology curriculum. \n Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. \n A commitment to student-centered learning, academic excellence, and faculty \ncollaboration. \nQualifications for Tenure-Track Appointment \nPreference will be given to candidates holding an earned terminal degree, including but not \nlimited to: \n Ph.D. in Biology or a related biological science \n Doctor of Medicine (MD) \n Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) \n Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) \n Other appropriate earned doctoral degree in a closely related discipline \nCandidates who are ABD or nearing completion of a terminal degree may be considered, with \nappointment status determined according to university policies. \nAdditional preferred qualifications include: \n Experience teaching undergraduate laboratory courses. \n Clinical experience as a physician (MD or DO), advanced practice registered nurse \n(APRN), nurse practitioner, physician assistant, or other healthcare professional. \n Experience mentoring undergraduate research, internships, or experiential learning. \n Commitment to active-learning strategies and innovative instructional methods. \n Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration with programs such as Nursing, Exercise \nScience, Psychology, Education, Chemistry, and Environmental Science. \n Demonstrated commitment to student success, mentorship, and community engagement. \n \n \n \n \nAbout Union Commonwealth University \nUnion Commonwealth University is a private, liberal arts institution located in Barbourville, \nKentucky, with a longstanding commitment to educating students for meaningful lives and \ncareers. Founded in the Appalachian region, Union combines personalized education with \nopportunities for students to engage deeply with their communities and the wider world. Our \nfaculty are dedicated teachers, mentors, and scholars who value close student relationships, \nclassroom innovation, and the transformative power of higher education.  \nApplication Process \nApplicants should submit: \n Letter of application addressing qualifications and interest in the position \n Curriculum vitae \n Statement of teaching philosophy \n Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon appointment) \n Contact information for three professional references \nApplications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. \nUnion Commonwealth University (the \"University\") is committed to maintaining an educational, \nemployment, and business environment free of all forms of discrimination. The University \nprovides full and equal access to its educational services, classes, and programs without regard to \nand prohibits discrimination based on the protected characteristics of age (40 and older), race, \ncolor, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex (including transgender status, gender identity or \nexpression), pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation, and related medical conditions), physical \nor mental disability, AIDS/HIV status, genetic information (including testing and \ncharacteristics), veteran status, uniformed servicemember status, status as a smoker or \nnonsmoker, medical condition, sexual orientation, marital status, or because an individual is \nperceived to have one or more of the foregoing characteristics, or any other status protected by \nfederal, state, or local laws. \n "
    },
    "https://irp.cdn-website.com/62fe7d2a/files/uploaded/Assistant+Professor+of+Exercise+Science.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Exercise Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Exercise Science.  \n \nAssistant Professor of Exercise Science \nFull-Time, Tenure-Track Position \n \nUnion Commonwealth University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor \nof Exercise Science beginning January 15, 2026. We seek an engaged, student-centered \nteacher of exercise science who helps students connect the science of human movement \nto the health of the people and communities they will serve, and who takes seriously the \nwork of teaching that science to undergraduates in their first laboratory course. \n \nThe successful candidate will join a growing academic community committed to \nstudent-centered learning, professional preparation, and the liberal arts tradition. The \nposition carries a substantial and valued role in preparing students for graduate and \nprofessional study in the health sciences and for careers in clinical, fitness, and wellness \nsettings, along with the opportunity to shape a developing Exercise Science curriculum \nthrough upper-division teaching, laboratory instruction, advising, and program \ndevelopment. \n \nThe appointment is tenure-track, contingent upon the successful candidate holding an \nearned terminal degree in Exercise Science or a closely related field at the time of \nappointment. \n \nAreas of Specialization \nSpecialization within the discipline is open, and we welcome candidates trained in \nexercise physiology, biomechanics, strength and conditioning, motor behavior, or \nclinical and applied exercise science. Candidates prepared to teach broadly across the \nExercise Science curriculum outside their own specialization are especially encouraged \nto apply. \n \nPosition Responsibilities \nThe successful candidate will: \n Teach foundational courses in the Exercise Science curriculum, with a \ncommitment to making the classroom and the laboratory a genuine intellectual \nexperience rather than a requirement students endure. \n\n Teach courses that prepare students for professional certification and for \ngraduate and professional programs in the health sciences, working closely with \ncolleagues in related programs on curricular alignment. \n Develop and teach upper-division courses in the candidate's area of \nspecialization, including a signature laboratory-based course. \n Mentor and advise Exercise Science majors and minors, and direct \nundergraduate research, internships, and practicum experiences. \n Participate in assessment, curriculum development, academic advising, and \nuniversity service. \n Maintain an active program of scholarship appropriate to the discipline and to a \nteaching-centered institution. \n \nRequired Qualifications \n Earned doctorate (Ph.D., Ed.D., or equivalent) in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, \nExercise Physiology, Biomechanics, or a closely related field by the time of \nappointment. ABD candidates nearing completion may be considered, with \nappointment status determined by degree completion timeline and institutional \nneeds. \n Evidence of effective teaching, or strong potential for teaching, at the \nundergraduate level. \n Demonstrated ability to teach foundational exercise science courses, including \nlaboratory instruction, and to contribute broadly across the curriculum. \n Commitment to undergraduate education, student mentorship, and inclusive \nlearning environments. \n \nPreferred Qualifications \n Research or teaching expertise in exercise physiology, biomechanics, or strength \nand conditioning. \n Experience teaching laboratory courses involving exercise testing, fitness \nassessment, or related hands-on instruction. \n Current professional certification relevant to the position, such as ACSM-CEP, \nACSM-EP, or NSCA-CSCS. \n Experience with undergraduate research mentorship, internship supervision, or \nproject-based learning. \n Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration and community engagement, including \npartnerships with healthcare, wellness, and school organizations. \n \nAbout Union Commonwealth University \nUnion Commonwealth University is a private, liberal arts institution located in \nBarbourville, Kentucky, with a longstanding commitment to educating students for \nmeaningful lives and careers. Founded in the Appalachian region, Union combines \npersonalized education with opportunities for students to engage deeply with their \ncommunities and the wider world. \n \nOur faculty are dedicated teachers, mentors, and scholars who value close student \nrelationships, classroom innovation, and the transformative power of higher education. \n \nApplication Process \nApplicants should submit: \n Letter of application addressing qualifications and interest in the position \n Curriculum vitae \n Statement of teaching philosophy \n Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon appointment) \n Contact information for three professional references \n \nScreening of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \nOfficial transcripts and a satisfactory background check will be required before \nappointment. \n \nInterested candidates should submit a cover letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and the \ncontact information for three professional references to: \nHumanResources@unionky.edu & facultyhiring@unionky.edu \n \nFounded in 1879, Union is a small, liberal-arts institution located in southeastern \nKentucky. Union boasts a long commitment to Appalachia, providing quality education \nto a wide range of students from across the world, while maintaining a focus on the \nunderserved and marginalized, especially first-generation college students. \n \nUnion Commonwealth University (the “University”) is committed to maintaining an \neducational, employment, and business environment free of all forms of discrimination. \nThe University provides full and equal access to its educational services, classes, and \nprograms without regard to and prohibits discrimination based on the protected \ncharacteristics of age (40 and older), race, color, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex \n(including transgender status, gender identity or expression), pregnancy (including \nchildbirth, lactation, and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, \nAIDS/HIV status, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran \nstatus, uniformed servicemember status, status as a smoker or nonsmoker, medical \ncondition, sexual orientation, marital status, or because an individual is perceived to \nhave one or more of the foregoing characteristics, or any other status protected by \nfederal, state, or local laws "
    },
    "https://irp.cdn-website.com/62fe7d2a/files/uploaded/Assistant+Professor+of+Health+Sciences-cda459b9.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences.  \n \n \nFull-Time Non-Tenure Track Position \nAssistant Professor of Health Sciences \n \nUnion Commonwealth University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track \nAssistant Professor of Health Sciences beginning August 11, 2026. \nThe successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in \nundergraduate teaching, student mentoring, academic advising, curriculum \ndevelopment, recruitment and retention, professional development, and service to the \nDepartment, School, and University. \nApplicants from diverse academic and professional backgrounds are encouraged to \napply, including those with expertise in biology, biomedical sciences, medicine, nursing, \nanatomy and physiology, microbiology, public health, physician assistant studies, allied \nhealth, and other health-related disciplines. \nThe successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate courses in the biological \nand health sciences based on departmental needs and the candidate's academic \npreparation, professional background, and areas of expertise. The position provides an \nopportunity to contribute across multiple programs and support students preparing for \ncareers in healthcare and the health sciences. \nPosition Responsibilities \n Teach courses such as General Biology, Human Biology, Anatomy and \nPhysiology, Microbiology, and other health science courses appropriate to the \ncandidate's graduate preparation and professional experience. \n Contribute to courses and academic programs related to healthcare, nursing, pre-\nprofessional studies, and other health-related fields as academically qualified. \n Develop engaging learning experiences that connect scientific principles with \nhealthcare, clinical practice, evidence-based decision-making, and current \nresearch. \n Foster critical thinking, scientific inquiry, laboratory skills, and the application of \nscientific knowledge to health and healthcare. \n Advise and mentor students pursuing careers in medicine, nursing, physician \nassistant studies, physical therapy, occupational therapy, allied health, public \nhealth, and other health professions. \n Participate in curriculum assessment and development, program development, \nstudent recruitment and retention, and academic advising. \n Collaborate with faculty across Biology, Nursing, and other academic programs to \nsupport interdisciplinary education and student success. \n Contribute to departmental, University, and professional service activities. \n \n \n \n \n Maintain ongoing professional development, scholarship, research, or clinical \npractice appropriate to the individual's discipline and faculty appointment. \nRequired Qualifications \nApplicants must possess: \n An earned master's degree or higher in Nursing (SRNP), Biology, Biomedical \nSciences, Medicine, Physiology, Microbiology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or another \nclosely related life science discipline by the time of appointment.  \n Graduate education, professional credentials, and/or relevant professional \nexperience appropriate to the courses assigned.  \n Evidence of successful college-level teaching or demonstrated potential for \nexcellence in undergraduate instruction.  \n Ability to teach undergraduate courses in one or more areas of biology, health \nsciences, exercise science, health promotion, or related disciplines, consistent \nwith the candidate’s academic preparation and professional expertise.  \n Ability and willingness to contribute across multiple areas of the undergraduate \nhealth science curriculum.  \n Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills.  \n A commitment to student-centered learning, academic excellence, \ninterdisciplinary collaboration, and faculty collegiality. \nAbout Union Commonwealth University \nUnion Commonwealth University is a private, liberal arts institution located in \nBarbourville, Kentucky, with a longstanding commitment to educating students for \nmeaningful lives and careers. Founded in the Appalachian region, Union combines \npersonalized education with opportunities for students to engage deeply with their \ncommunities and the wider world. Our faculty are dedicated teachers, mentors, and \nscholars who value close student relationships, classroom innovation, and the \ntransformative power of higher education.  \nApplication Process \nApplicants should submit: \n Letter of application addressing qualifications and interest in the position \n Curriculum vitae \n Statement of teaching philosophy \n Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon appointment) \n Contact information for three professional references \nApplications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. \n \n \n \nUnion Commonwealth University (the \"University\") is committed to maintaining an \neducational, employment, and business environment free of all forms of discrimination. \nThe University provides full and equal access to its educational services, classes, and \nprograms without regard to and prohibits discrimination based on the protected \ncharacteristics of age (40 and older), race, color, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex \n(including transgender status, gender identity or expression), pregnancy (including \nchildbirth, lactation, and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, \nAIDS/HIV status, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran \nstatus, uniformed servicemember status, status as a smoker or nonsmoker, medical \ncondition, sexual orientation, marital status, or because an individual is perceived to \nhave one or more of the foregoing characteristics, or any other status protected by \nfederal, state, or local laws. \n "
    },
    "https://irp.cdn-website.com/62fe7d2a/files/uploaded/History+Professor.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of History.  \n \nAssistant Professor of History (World History) \nFull-Time, Tenure-Track Position \n \nUnion Commonwealth University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor \nof History beginning January 15, 2027. We seek an engaged, student-centered teacher of \nworld history who helps students see the connections that have bound distant peoples \ntogether, and who takes the work of teaching those connections to undergraduates in \ntheir first college history course seriously. \n \nThe successful candidate will join a growing academic community committed to \nstudent-centered learning, professional preparation, and the liberal arts tradition. The \nposition carries a substantial and valued role in the university's general education core \nand in preparing our teacher candidates, along with the opportunity to shape a revised \nHistory curriculum through upper-division teaching, advising, and program \ndevelopment. \nThe appointment is tenure-track, contingent upon the successful candidate holding an \nearned terminal degree in History or a closely related field at the time of appointment. \n \nAreas of Specialization \nWe privilege applications from candidates whose training and research engage the \nAtlantic World. Period and regional focus within that frame are open, and we welcome \ncandidates working in African, European, Caribbean, or American contexts, and in any \nera from the early modern period forward. Candidates prepared to teach broadly in \nworld history outside their own specialization are especially encouraged to apply. \n \nPosition Responsibilities \nThe successful candidate will: \n Teach the world history survey sequence as a core contribution to the university's \ngeneral education program, with a commitment to making those courses a \ngenuine intellectual experience rather than a requirement students endure. \n Teach world history content courses that serve our Education students and \nsupport Social Studies certification, working closely with colleagues in the \nEducation program on curricular alignment. \n Develop and teach upper-division courses in the candidate's area of \nspecialization, including a signature course in the Atlantic World. \n\n Mentor and advise History majors and minors, and direct undergraduate \nresearch through the program's methods and capstone sequence. \n Participate in assessment, curriculum development, academic advising, and \nuniversity service. \n Maintain an active program of scholarship appropriate to the discipline and to a \nteaching-centered institution. \n \nRequired Qualifications \n Earned Ph.D. in History or a closely related field by the time of appointment. \nABD candidates nearing completion may be considered, with appointment status \ndetermined by degree completion timeline and institutional needs. \n Evidence of effective teaching, or strong potential for teaching, at the \nundergraduate level. \n Demonstrated ability to teach the world history survey and to contribute broadly \nacross the History curriculum. \n Commitment to undergraduate education, student mentorship, and inclusive \nlearning environments. \n \nPreferred Qualifications \n Research or teaching expertise in the Atlantic World. \n Experience teaching general education courses to non-majors. \n Familiarity with teacher preparation, Social Studies content standards, or \ncollaboration with education faculty. \n Experience with dual credit instruction, undergraduate research mentorship, or \nproject-based learning. \n Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration and community engagement. \n \nAbout Union Commonwealth University \nUnion Commonwealth University is a private, liberal arts institution located in \nBarbourville, Kentucky, with a longstanding commitment to educating students for \nmeaningful lives and careers. Founded in the Appalachian region, Union combines \npersonalized education with opportunities for students to engage deeply with their \ncommunities and the wider world. \nOur faculty are dedicated teachers, mentors, and scholars who value close student \nrelationships, classroom innovation, and the transformative power of higher education. \n \nApplication Process \nApplicants should submit: \n Letter of application addressing qualifications and interest in the position \n Curriculum vitae \n Statement of teaching philosophy \n Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon appointment) \n Contact information for three professional references \n \n \n \nScreening of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.  \n \nInterested candidates should submit a cover letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and the \ncontact information for three professional references to: \nHumanResources@unionky.edu & facultyhiring@unionky.edu \n \nFounded in 1879, Union is a small, liberal-arts institution located in southeastern \nKentucky. Union boasts a long commitment to Appalachia, providing quality education \nto a wide range of students from across the world, while maintaining a focus on the \nunderserved and marginalized, especially first-generation college students.  \n \nUnion Commonwealth University (the \"University\") is committed to maintaining an \neducational, employment, and business environment free of all forms of discrimination. \nThe University provides full and equal access to its educational services, classes, and \nprograms without regard to and prohibits discrimination based on the protected \ncharacteristics of age (40 and older), race, color, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex \n(including transgender status, gender identity or expression), pregnancy (including \nchildbirth, lactation, and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, \nAIDS/HIV status, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran \nstatus, uniformed servicemember status, status as a smoker or nonsmoker, medical \ncondition, sexual orientation, marital status, or because an individual is perceived to \nhave one or more of the foregoing characteristics, or any other status protected by \nfederal, state, or local laws \n \n "
    }
